Chapter: RvArgOrder
  cites Foreword chapter Console

Section: Probes

  f-two : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  f-two (a) (b) = a - b

  seven : Integer
  seven = 7

 `f-bin` is deliberately NOT the discriminating case and is kept as the
 control: `x` is a parameter, so it sits in a callee-saved register and a
 call cannot reach it. `f-bin2` is the real one. Its left operand is an
 expression, so it lands in a caller-saved temp, and the call to `seven` on
 the right is then free to destroy it before the subtraction reads it.

  f-bin : Integer -> Integer
  f-bin (x) = x - seven

  f-bin2 : Integer -> Integer
  f-bin2 (x) = (x * 2) - seven

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line-uni ("lit-lit: " & show (f-two 7 2))
   print-line-uni ("call-lit: " & show (f-two seven 2))
   print-line-uni ("lit-call: " & show (f-two 2 seven))
   print-line-uni ("bin-call: " & show (f-bin 10))
   print-line-uni ("bin2-call: " & show (f-bin2 10))
  end
